&lt;p&gt;Recommendations can include exploring with cancer survivors job accommodation ideas that they think can help improve their transition to work and optimize their productivity. While decisions on how to adjust for restrictions and limitations commonly lie with the employer, primary care providers can provide helpful suggestions and recommendations.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
The most helpful accommodations described by survivors, employers and health care providers are: graduated return to work, flexible scheduling, modification of physical work environment and provision of adaptive aids, modification of workplace duties and performance expectations and retraining and supports at the workplace (3).&lt;/p&gt;
